---
// /weihnachten-neujahr · /en/christmas-new-year
// All figures come from the forecast model at build time (and from the SSR
// forecast-range marker per request); nothing here is a hand-typed statistic.
// Next season: bump SEASON (dates + label) once the holidays are over.
import GuideLayout from './GuideLayout.astro';
import ForecastRange from './ForecastRange.astro';
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import { t, type Lang } from '../lib/i18n';
import { routePath } from '../lib/routes';
import { forecastRange, worstDay, busySpan, waitRange, hhmm, easterSundayIso, shiftIso, BUSY_MIN, type DayPeak } from '../lib/forecast-range';
import observed from '../data/observed-days.json';
import profiles from '../data/empirical-profiles.json';

interface Props {
  lang: Lang;
}
const { lang } = Astro.props;
const L = (de: string, en: string) => (lang === 'de' ? de : en);
const unit = t(lang, 'portal.minutes');

const SEASON = { from: '2026-12-19', to: '2027-01-04', label: '2026/27' };
const days = forecastRange(SEASON.from, SEASON.to, lang);

const dayName = (d: DayPeak) => `${d.fullDayLabel}, ${d.dateLabel}`;
const list = (items: string[]) =>
  items.length <= 1 ? items.join('') : `${items.slice(0, -1).join(', ')} ${L('und', 'and')} ${items[items.length - 1]}`;

// End a sentence after a list without doubling the date's own period ("29.12.").
const stop = (s: string) => (s.endsWith('.') ? s : s + '.');

const worstN = worstDay(days, 'north');
const worstS = worstDay(days, 'south');
// Days within a minute of the worst one (the model repeats its weekly pattern).
const topDays = (dir: 'north' | 'south', worst: DayPeak) => days.filter((d) => d[dir].typ >= worst[dir].typ - 1).map(dayName);
const peakOf = (d: DayPeak) => Math.max(d.north.typ, d.south.typ);
const quietest = [...days].sort((a, b) => peakOf(a) - peakOf(b) || a.isoDate.localeCompare(b.isoDate)).slice(0, 3)
  .sort((a, b) => a.isoDate.localeCompare(b.isoDate));
const span = busySpan(days);
const seasonMax = Math.max(...days.map(peakOf));
const holidayStart = days.find((d) => d.context);
// Same weekday as the worst southbound day, but before the holiday window.
const baseline = days.find((d) => !d.context && d.fullDayLabel === worstN.fullDayLabel);

// Easter of the following spring with the same model, for scale.
const easterYear = Number(SEASON.to.slice(0, 4));
const easterIso = easterSundayIso(easterYear);
const easterDays = forecastRange(shiftIso(easterIso, -4), shiftIso(easterIso, 8), lang);
const easterMax = Math.max(...easterDays.map(peakOf));

const measuredSince = new Date(observed.meta.firstReading).toLocaleDateString(lang === 'de' ? 'de-CH' : 'en-GB', { month: 'long', year: 'numeric', timeZone: 'Europe/Zurich' });
const tcsFrom = profiles.meta.dateStart.slice(0, 4);
const tcsTo = profiles.meta.dateEnd.slice(0, 4);

const hh = (h: number) => `${String(h).padStart(2, '0')}:00`;
const quietText = span
  ? L(`vor ${hh(span[0])} oder ab ${hh(span[1] + 1)} Uhr`, `before ${hh(span[0])} or from ${hh(span[1] + 1)}`)
  : L('zu jeder Tageszeit', 'at any time of day');

const title = t(lang, 'meta.christmas.title').replace('{season}', SEASON.label);
const description = t(lang, 'meta.christmas.description').replace('{season}', SEASON.label);
const h1 = L(`Gotthard-Stau an Weihnachten und Neujahr ${SEASON.label}`, `Gotthard traffic at Christmas and New Year ${SEASON.label}`);
const intro = L(
  `Wie voll wird der Gotthard über die Festtage? Unsere Prognose für jeden Tag vom ${days[0].dateLabel} bis ${days[days.length - 1].dateLabel}, getrennt nach Richtung, mit den ruhigsten Zeiten zum Fahren.`,
  `How busy will the Gotthard be over the holidays? Our forecast for every day from ${days[0].dateLabel} to ${days[days.length - 1].dateLabel}, by direction, with the quietest times to drive.`,
);

const faq = [
  {
    q: L('Wann ist an Weihnachten und Neujahr am Gotthard am meisten Stau?', 'When is Gotthard traffic worst at Christmas and New Year?'),
    a: L(
      `Laut unserer Prognose Richtung Süden (Göschenen) am ${list(topDays('north', worstN))} mit typisch ${waitRange(worstN.north)} Minuten Wartezeit gegen ${hhmm(worstN.north.minute)} Uhr, Richtung Norden (Airolo) am ${list(topDays('south', worstS))} mit ${waitRange(worstS.south)} Minuten gegen ${hhmm(worstS.south.minute)} Uhr.`,
      `According to our forecast, southbound (Göschenen) on ${list(topDays('north', worstN))} with typically ${waitRange(worstN.north)} minutes of waiting around ${hhmm(worstN.north.minute)}, and northbound (Airolo) on ${list(topDays('south', worstS))} with ${waitRange(worstS.south)} minutes around ${hhmm(worstS.south.minute)}.`,
    ),
  },
  {
    q: L('Wann fahre ich über die Festtage am besten durch den Gotthard?', 'When is the best time to drive through the Gotthard over the holidays?'),
    a: L(
      `Am ruhigsten ${quietText}: Dann erwartet das Modell an allen Tagen weniger als ${BUSY_MIN} Minuten Wartezeit. Die ruhigsten Tage sind ${stop(list(quietest.map(dayName)))}`,
      `Quietest ${quietText}: the model expects less than ${BUSY_MIN} minutes of waiting then on every day. The quietest days are ${stop(list(quietest.map(dayName)))}`,
    ),
  },
  {
    q: L('Ist der Gotthardpass über Weihnachten offen?', 'Is the Gotthard Pass open over Christmas?'),
    a: L(
      'Nein. Die Passstrasse ist im Winter geschlossen, etwa von November bis Mai. Über die Festtage führt der Weg durch den Strassentunnel.',
      'No. The pass road is closed in winter, roughly from November to May. Over the holidays the route is through the road tunnel.',
    ),
  },
  {
    q: L('Wie zuverlässig ist die Weihnachtsprognose?', 'How reliable is the Christmas forecast?'),
    a: L(
      `Es ist eine Modellrechnung aus Wochentag, Saison und Ferienkalender, kalibriert mit unseren eigenen Messungen seit ${measuredSince}. Für Weihnachten selbst haben wir noch keine Messwerte. Unfälle, Pannen und Schneefall können die Lage stark verändern, deshalb vor der Fahrt die Live-Werte prüfen.`,
      `It is a model based on weekday, season and holiday calendar, calibrated with our own measurements since ${measuredSince}. We have no measurements of Christmas itself yet. Accidents, breakdowns and snowfall can change the picture quickly, so check the live values before you set off.`,
    ),
  },
];
---

<GuideLayout lang={lang} guide="christmas" title={title} description={description} h1={h1} intro={intro} faq={faq} dataSource={L('Verkehrsmodell (ASTRA-Daten)', 'Traffic model (ASTRA data)')}>
  <Fragment slot="top">
    <div class="tiles">
      <div class="tile">
        <span class="tile__label">{L('Stärkster Tag Richtung Süden', 'Busiest day southbound')}</span>
        <span class="tile__value">{worstN.fullDayLabel.slice(0, lang === 'de' ? 2 : 3)} {worstN.dateLabel}</span>
        <span class="tile__note">{L('ca.', 'about')} {waitRange(worstN.north)} {unit} {L('gegen', 'around')} {hhmm(worstN.north.minute)} · Göschenen</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <span class="tile__label">{L('Stärkster Tag Richtung Norden', 'Busiest day northbound')}</span>
        <span class="tile__value">{worstS.fullDayLabel.slice(0, lang === 'de' ? 2 : 3)} {worstS.dateLabel}</span>
        <span class="tile__note">{L('ca.', 'about')} {waitRange(worstS.south)} {unit} {L('gegen', 'around')} {hhmm(worstS.south.minute)} · Airolo</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <span class="tile__label">{L('Ruhigste Reisezeit', 'Quietest time to travel')}</span>
        <span class="tile__value">{span ? `${hh(span[1] + 1)}–${hh(span[0])}` : L('ganztags', 'all day')}</span>
        <span class="tile__note">{L(`an allen Tagen unter ${BUSY_MIN} ${unit} erwartet`, `under ${BUSY_MIN} ${unit} expected on every day`)}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="xmas-days-title">
      <div class="section__titles">
        <h2 class="section__title" id="xmas-days-title">{L('Prognose pro Tag', 'Forecast by day')}</h2>
        <p class="section__sub">{L('Erwartete Spitzenwartezeit an einem typischen Tag, je Richtung, mit Uhrzeit der Spitze. An starken Tagen kann es deutlich mehr sein.', 'Expected peak wait on a typical day, per direction, with the time of the peak. Busy days can be considerably worse.')}</p>
      </div>
      <ForecastRange lang={lang} from={SEASON.from} to={SEASON.to} />
      <p class="section__note">{t(lang, 'forecast.disclaimer')} <a href={routePath('forecasts', lang)}>{L('Tagesverlauf in der Prognose ansehen', 'See the hour-by-hour forecast')}</a></p>
    </section>
  </Fragment>

  <section class="section prose" aria-labelledby="xmas-when-title">
    <h2 class="section__title" id="xmas-when-title">{L('Wann ist über die Festtage am meisten Stau?', 'When are the queues worst over the holidays?')}</h2>
    {lang === 'de' ? (
      <p>Richtung Süden, also vor dem Nordportal in Göschenen, erwartet unser Modell die längsten Wartezeiten am {list(topDays('north', worstN))}: typisch rund {worstN.north.typ} Minuten, an einem starken Tag bis {worstN.north.high} Minuten, mit der Spitze gegen {hhmm(worstN.north.minute)} Uhr. Richtung Norden, vor dem Südportal in Airolo, ist es am {list(topDays('south', worstS))} am vollsten ({waitRange(worstS.south)} Minuten gegen {hhmm(worstS.south.minute)} Uhr). Das entspricht dem üblichen Wochenrhythmus am Gotthard: Hinreise in den Süden vor und am Wochenende, Rückreise am Sonntagnachmittag.</p>
    ) : (
      <p>Southbound, in front of the north portal at Göschenen, our model expects the longest waits on {list(topDays('north', worstN))}: typically around {worstN.north.typ} minutes, up to {worstN.north.high} minutes on a busy day, peaking around {hhmm(worstN.north.minute)}. Northbound, in front of the south portal at Airolo, {list(topDays('south', worstS))} {topDays('south', worstS).length > 1 ? 'are' : 'is'} the busiest ({waitRange(worstS.south)} minutes around {hhmm(worstS.south.minute)}). That follows the usual weekly rhythm at the Gotthard: outbound trips south before and at the weekend, return trips on Sunday afternoon.</p>
    )}
    {lang === 'de' ? (
      <p>Der Grund sind die Weihnachtsferien in der Schweiz und den Nachbarländern. Unser Kalendermodell rechnet {holidayStart ? `ab dem ${holidayStart.dateLabel}` : 'über die Festtage'} mit Ferienverkehr{baseline ? `; zum Vergleich: am ${dayName(baseline)}, noch vor den Ferien, erwartet es Richtung Süden nur rund ${baseline.north.typ} Minuten` : ''}. Trotzdem bleibt der Winter am Gotthard ruhig im Vergleich zu Ostern oder dem Sommer: Über die Festtage erwartet das Modell höchstens rund {seasonMax} Minuten, an Ostern {easterYear} bis zu {easterMax} Minuten.</p>
    ) : (
      <p>The reason is the Christmas school holidays in Switzerland and its neighbouring countries. Our calendar model treats {holidayStart ? `the days from ${holidayStart.dateLabel}` : 'the holidays'} as holiday traffic{baseline ? `; for comparison, on ${dayName(baseline)}, before the holidays start, it expects only around ${baseline.north.typ} minutes southbound` : ''}. Even so, winter at the Gotthard stays calm compared with Easter or summer: over Christmas the model expects at most around {seasonMax} minutes, at Easter {easterYear} up to {easterMax} minutes.</p>
    )}
  </section>

  <section class="section prose" aria-labelledby="xmas-best-title">
    <h2 class="section__title" id="xmas-best-title">{L('Wann fahre ich am besten?', 'When should I drive?')}</h2>
    <ul>
      {lang === 'de' ? (
        <>
          <li><strong>Früh oder spät:</strong> {span ? `Vor ${hh(span[0])} und ab ${hh(span[1] + 1)} Uhr` : 'Den ganzen Tag'} erwartet das Modell an allen Tagen weniger als {BUSY_MIN} Minuten Wartezeit.</li>
          <li><strong>Ruhige Tage wählen:</strong> Am wenigsten los ist am {stop(list(quietest.map(dayName)))}</li>
          <li><strong>Spitzentage meiden:</strong> Richtung Süden nicht am {list(topDays('north', worstN))} um die Mittagszeit, Richtung Norden nicht am {list(topDays('south', worstS))} am Nachmittag.</li>
          <li><strong>Kurz vor der Abfahrt nachsehen:</strong> Unfälle, Pannen und Schnee verändern die Lage schnell. Die <a href={routePath('home', lang)}>Live-Werte für beide Portale</a> werden alle paar Minuten aktualisiert.</li>
        </>
      ) : (
        <>
          <li><strong>Early or late:</strong> {span ? `before ${hh(span[0])} and from ${hh(span[1] + 1)}` : 'all day'}, the model expects less than {BUSY_MIN} minutes of waiting on every day.</li>
          <li><strong>Pick quiet days:</strong> the quietest are {stop(list(quietest.map(dayName)))}</li>
          <li><strong>Avoid the peaks:</strong> southbound not on {list(topDays('north', worstN))} around midday, northbound not on {list(topDays('south', worstS))} in the afternoon.</li>
          <li><strong>Check just before you leave:</strong> accidents, breakdowns and snow change the picture quickly. The <a href={routePath('home', lang)}>live values for both portals</a> refresh every few minutes.</li>
        </>
      )}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose" aria-labelledby="xmas-history-title">
    <h2 class="section__title" id="xmas-history-title">{L('Was zeigen frühere Jahre?', 'What do past years show?')}</h2>
    {lang === 'de' ? (
      <p>Ehrlich gesagt: noch wenig. Unsere eigenen ASTRA-Messungen am Tunnel laufen seit {measuredSince}, die Festtage {SEASON.label} sind also die ersten, die wir selbst messen. Die ausgewerteten TCS-Staumeldungen {tcsFrom}–{tcsTo} enthalten keine eigene Weihnachtsauswertung. Diese Prognose stützt sich deshalb auf unser gemessenes Wochenprofil und den Ferienkalender. Nach den Festtagen fliessen die Messungen in die <a href={routePath('statistics', lang)}>Statistik</a> und in die nächste Prognose ein.</p>
    ) : (
      <p>Honestly: not much yet. Our own ASTRA measurements at the tunnel have been running since {measuredSince}, so the {SEASON.label} holidays are the first we measure ourselves. The TCS traffic reports {tcsFrom}–{tcsTo} that we analysed contain no separate Christmas effect. This forecast therefore rests on our measured weekly profile and the holiday calendar. After the holidays the measurements feed into the <a href={routePath('statistics', lang)}>statistics</a> and the next forecast.</p>
    )}
    <p class="callout"><Icon name="snow" />{L('Im Winter ist die Gotthard-Passstrasse geschlossen; als Ausweichroute bleibt vor allem der San Bernardino (A13).', 'In winter the Gotthard Pass road is closed; the main alternative is the San Bernardino (A13).')}</p>
  </section>
</GuideLayout>
